IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch02-08`

-- Tests for chapters 2 to 8.  Every expected value was written from the text before the
-- file was run; unit ids (2.1, 7.3 ...) are those of the coverage table in NOTES.md.
-- Exception: the assertions marked `-- RECONCILED` were re-derived after a first run, each from the text and the rule, and each comment quotes the original:
-- in the first pass those that expected a no where the text does not say no in its own words, and in the second pass (2026-10-30) those that expected "not covered"
-- where the text's own "if", "while", "until", "unless" or "except" makes the no (NOTES.md, "Where the text says no, and where it does not").

§ `Tests -- chapters 2 to 8`

§§ `Chapter 2 -- the holder is within the chapter`

-- 2.1: "any of our earls or barons, or others holding of us in chief by military service".
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the holder is one of those this chapter speaks of` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the holder is one of those this chapter speaks of` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the holder is one of those this chapter speaks of` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 2 -- the holder is one of those this chapter speaks of` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Chapter 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief`

-- 2.1: argument order is earl-or-baron, in chief by military service, holder died, heir of full age, heir owes relief, relief paid.
-- An earl died; the heir is of full age, owes relief and has paid: he has his inheritance.
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- Relief not yet paid: "on payment of" says what the heir has once he pays and nothing of the heir who has not paid (not covered).
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- An "other" holding in chief by military service is within the chapter.
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- Neither an earl or baron nor a tenant in chief by military service: the chapter does not speak.
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- The holder has not died.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`
-- The heir is not of full age (chapter 3 is the chapter for that case).
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`
-- The heir does not owe relief.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`

§§ `Chapter 2 -- the sums`

-- 2.2, 2.3, 2.4: GBP 100 for an earl's barony, GBP 100 for a barony, 100s for a knight's fee.
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the sum the Charter names for a whole holding of this kind` `a whole earl's barony` EQUALS Pounds 100
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the sum the Charter names for a whole holding of this kind` `a whole barony` EQUALS Pounds 100
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the sum the Charter names for a whole holding of this kind` `a whole knight's fee` EQUALS Shillings 100

-- 2.5: "whoever owes less let him give less".  Owing nothing less: the named sum.
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `a whole earl's barony` NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Pounds 100)
-- Owing 60 by the custom of the fief: 60.
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `a whole earl's barony` (JUST 60) EQUALS JUST (Pounds 60)
-- Boundary: owing exactly the named sum gives the named sum.
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `a whole earl's barony` (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST (Pounds 100)
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `a whole barony` NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Pounds 100)
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `a whole barony` (JUST 99) EQUALS JUST (Pounds 99)
-- Owing more by custom than the sum the Charter names: the Charter's sum.
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `a whole barony` (JUST 150) EQUALS JUST (Pounds 100)
-- 2.4: for a knight's fee the text names a ceiling only, so with nothing owed by custom it states no sum.
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `a whole knight's fee` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `a whole knight's fee` (JUST 40) EQUALS JUST (Shillings 40)
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `a whole knight's fee` (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST (Shillings 100)
-- "100s. at most": above the ceiling, the ceiling.
#ASSERT `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `a whole knight's fee` (JUST 120) EQUALS JUST (Shillings 100)

§§ `Chapter 3 -- an heir who was in wardship`

-- 3.1: argument order is earl-or-baron, in chief, heir was a minor in wardship, heir has come of age.
#ASSERT `ch 3 -- relief or a fine may be demanded of the heir on coming of age` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 3 -- relief or a fine may be demanded of the heir on coming of age` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- Not in wardship: the chapter does not speak (chapter 2 does).
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 3 -- relief or a fine may be demanded of the heir on coming of age` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 3 -- relief or a fine may be demanded of the heir on coming of age` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Not yet of age.
#ASSERT `ch 3 -- relief or a fine may be demanded of the heir on coming of age` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- Not one of "the aforesaid".
#ASSERT `ch 3 -- relief or a fine may be demanded of the heir on coming of age` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- 3.1: the King demands relief of such an heir: a breach.
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 3 -- the heir shall have his inheritance without relief and without fine` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `demand relief or a fine from an heir who was a minor in wardship` AT 5
-- expect: MUST NOT `demand relief or a fine from an heir who was a minor in wardship`
#TRACE `ch 3 -- the heir shall have his inheritance without relief and without fine` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- The heir was not in wardship: nothing in chapter 3 forbids the demand.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 3 -- the heir shall have his inheritance without relief and without fine` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `demand relief or a fine from an heir who was a minor in wardship` AT 5

§§ `Chapter 4 -- what the guardian may take, and waste`

-- 4.1: argument order is more than reasonable, with destruction or waste.
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- the guardian may take this from the heir's land` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- the guardian may take this from the heir's land` FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- the guardian may take this from the heir's land` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- the guardian may take this from the heir's land` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`

-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 4 -- the guardian shall take from the land nothing but reasonable produce, customs and services` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a guardian` DOES `take from the heir's land more than reasonable produce, reasonable customs and reasonable services` AT 3
-- expect: MUST NOT `take from the heir's land more than reasonable produce, reasonable customs and reasonable services`
#TRACE `ch 4 -- the guardian shall take from the land nothing but reasonable produce, customs and services` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 4 -- the guardian shall not make destruction or waste of men or goods` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a guardian` DOES `make destruction or waste of the men or goods of the wardship` AT 3
-- expect: MUST NOT `make destruction or waste of the men or goods of the wardship`
#TRACE `ch 4 -- the guardian shall not make destruction or waste of men or goods` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100

-- 4.2: a wardship committed to the sheriff or another accountable to the King: amends and two men.
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- the consequence for a guardian of this kind who has made waste` `committed by the King to the sheriff or another accountable to him` EQUALS `The King takes amends and the land is committed to two lawful and discreet men of that fee`
-- 4.4: a wardship given or sold: the guardian loses it and it is transferred to two men.
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- the consequence for a guardian of this kind who has made waste` `given or sold by the King to someone` EQUALS `The wardship is lost and transferred to two lawful and discreet men of that fief`
-- No waste: nothing follows under the chapter.
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- what follows if the guardian lays waste` `given or sold by the King to someone` FALSE EQUALS `Nothing follows under chapter 4`
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- what follows if the guardian lays waste` `committed by the King to the sheriff or another accountable to him` FALSE EQUALS `Nothing follows under chapter 4`
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- what follows if the guardian lays waste` `given or sold by the King to someone` TRUE EQUALS `The wardship is lost and transferred to two lawful and discreet men of that fief`
#ASSERT `ch 4 -- what follows if the guardian lays waste` `committed by the King to the sheriff or another accountable to him` TRUE EQUALS `The King takes amends and the land is committed to two lawful and discreet men of that fee`

§§ `Chapter 5 -- upkeep and restoration`

-- 5.1: the guardian "shall keep up" the houses ...: the duty stands until done (the text gives no time).
-- expect: MUST `keep up the houses, parks, places for live-stock, fishponds, mills and other things pertaining to the land`
#TRACE `ch 5 -- the guardian shall keep up the houses, parks, fishponds, mills and other things out of the issues of the land` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 1000
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 5 -- the guardian shall keep up the houses, parks, fishponds, mills and other things out of the issues of the land` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a guardian` DOES `keep up the houses, parks, places for live-stock, fishponds, mills and other things pertaining to the land` AT 4

-- 5.2: the duty to restore arises "when he has come to full age".
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 5 -- the guardian shall restore the land to the heir who has come to full age` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: MUST `restore to the heir all his land, stocked with ploughs and implements of husbandry`
#TRACE `ch 5 -- the guardian shall restore the land to the heir who has come to full age` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 5 -- the guardian shall restore the land to the heir who has come to full age` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a guardian` DOES `restore to the heir all his land, stocked with ploughs and implements of husbandry` AT 7

-- 5.2: all his land, stocked, as the season requires and the issues can bear.
#ASSERT `ch 5 -- the restoration is what the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 5 -- the restoration is what the Charter requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 5 -- the restoration is what the Charter requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 5 -- the restoration is what the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§§ `Chapter 6 -- the marriage of the heir`

-- 6.1: argument order is disparagement, notice to the nearest in blood.
#ASSERT `ch 6 -- the heir may be married in this way` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 6 -- the heir may be married in this way` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 6 -- the heir may be married in this way` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- No disparagement and notice given: the chapter states what bars a marriage and says nothing of one that meets both (not covered).
#ASSERT `ch 6 -- the heir may be married in this way` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 7 -- the widow`

-- 7.1: after her husband's death she is to have her portion and inheritance without difficulty.
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the widow may be kept waiting or put to difficulty over her marriage portion and inheritance` TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the widow may be kept waiting or put to difficulty over her marriage portion and inheritance` FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- 7.2: she shall not give anything for her dower, her marriage portion or the joint inheritance.
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the widow may be made to give this` TRUE `something for her dower` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the widow may be made to give this` TRUE `something for her marriage portion` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the widow may be made to give this` TRUE `something for the inheritance which her husband and she held on the day of his death` EQUALS Barred
-- Any other payment is not mentioned.
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the widow may be made to give this` TRUE `some other payment` EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the widow may be made to give this` FALSE `something for her dower` EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- 7.3: "for forty days after his death".
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the number of days the widow may remain in her husband's house, within which her dower is assigned` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the widow may remain in her husband's house` 0 EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the widow may remain in her husband's house` 39 EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the widow may remain in her husband's house` 40 EQUALS Entitled
-- The text gives leave to remain for forty days and is silent about the forty-first day and about a day before the death (not covered).
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the widow may remain in her husband's house` 41 EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- the widow may remain in her husband's house` (0 MINUS 1) EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- 7.4: "within which time her dower shall be assigned".
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- her dower is assigned within the forty days` 0
#ASSERT `ch 7 -- her dower is assigned within the forty days` 40
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 7 -- her dower is assigned within the forty days` 41)

§§ `Chapter 8 -- no widow compelled to marry`

-- 8.1-8.2: argument order is she is a widow, prefers to live without a husband, gives security.
#ASSERT `ch 8 -- the widow may be compelled to marry` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- The proviso: no security, no protection under this chapter.
#ASSERT `ch 8 -- the widow may be compelled to marry` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- "so long as she prefers to live without a husband".
#ASSERT `ch 8 -- the widow may be compelled to marry` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 8 -- the widow may be compelled to marry` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- 8.2: against our consent if she holds of us, against the lord's if she holds of another.
#ASSERT `ch 8 -- the consent her security is against` TRUE EQUALS `the King's consent`
#ASSERT `ch 8 -- the consent her security is against` FALSE EQUALS `the consent of the lord of whom she holds`

-- assertions written: 69.  check.sh counts the assertions satisfied; the two must be equal.
